notified when a"] [122 1 "// callable handles it or it is blocked, else ignored or the default."] [149 1 "// killSignal is kill(pid, sig). The own process's signal with a Python handler, not blocked, is delivered here"] [150 1 "// and its handler run before kill returns, as the kernel delivers it to the calling thread before kill returns"] [151 1 "// (and SIGPROF, which Go's runtime keeps for itself, reaches the handler)."] [163 1 "// the interval timers (ITIMER_REAL, ITIMER_VIRTUAL, ITIMER_PROF), counted in wall time"] [177 1 "// setItimer arms which's timer (value 0 disarms), returning the old value and interval."] [196 3 "// disarmed: an expiry not yet handled is dropped, as the kernel's single pending bit is taken by the"] [197 3 "// handler that disarms it"] [217 5 "// a Python handler: delivered here, under the timer's lock, so a disarmed timer sends no more"] [218 5 "// (and SIGPROF, which Go's runtime keeps for itself, reaches it)"] [263 4 "// as at CPython's start: SIGINT's default_int_handler, SIGPIPE and SIGXFSZ ignored, the rest SIG_DFL"] [380 5 "// the C handler runs inside raise(): the Python handler before raise_signal returns"] [403 4 "// set_wakeup_fd(fd, /, *, warn_on_full_buffer=True)"] [512 5 "// only the main thread runs handlers: wait for any arrival"] [516 4 "// until a signal is pending (a stale wake-up token is not one)"] [569 7 "// delivered on unblocking: the default action or nothing"] [640 5 "// the own process's signal (a pidfd of another process times out here, harmlessly) handled"] [641 5 "// before the call returns, as the kernel delivers it"]] :go/pos {:name [1 9] :package [1 1]} :go/semis [[53 35] [73 26] [99 12] [99 22] [112 60] [142 22] [157 50] [265 14] [265 24] [302 31] [317 14] [317 24] [319 39] [344 40] [366 26] [386 63] [422 37] [439 32] [454 31] [496 37] [545 14] [545 24] [574 40] [605 40] [628 35] [636 104] [643 16] [643 61]]} (go/file "builtins_signal.go" :imports [


